# ws/net-n8 — scheduling and per-stream isolation in the eventfd pool

Three questions, three answers in one table:

1. **Does the eventfd pool still lose at N=8 after scheduling?** Yes, against
   the 1:1 path on the same tree: 34.93M against 54.26M (−35.6%), even though it
   serves 8/8 rings where the 1:1 path serves 7/8.
2. **Did this branch move N=1,2,4,8?** No, within the host's noise: pre→post at
   N=8 is +1.3%, and N≤4 is −1% to −5%.
3. **What is the lever?** Worker slots. With `max_worker_processes=16` the same
   eventfd image reaches 55.71M at 8/8; with `FASTPOSTGRES_RINGS_PER_WORKER=1`
   it reproduces the 7/8 shape at 53.60M. A portal is pinned to one worker, so
   dispatch order cannot remove the shared-worker turn.

Driver: `bench/internals/threads/ring_scaling.py`, N processes × one ring × three
object-free reads (`Cursor.aggregate`: columnar batches reduced in C++, no
Python object per row), 100000 rows per read, batch 25000. It is bind-mounted so
the SAME file runs on every image. Three rounds of six configs, one docker run
at a time under `/tmp/fpq-bench.lock`; each run is 3 reps and the tables below
are the medians of the three runs (raw values in brackets). The host had ~2
cores of background container load, which is the source of the ±5–10% at n≤4
and the one 42.66M n=8 outlier on the pre image.

### COMMAND (protocol baseline, `fpq-baseline` = main@7e3d2e6)

    flock /tmp/fpq-bench.lock -c 'docker run --rm --shm-size=3g \
      -e BENCH_GIT_REV=base \
      -v $PWD/bench/internals/threads/ring_scaling.py:/tmp/ring_scaling.py:ro \
      fpq-baseline python3 /tmp/ring_scaling.py --rows 100000 --reads 3 --reps 3'

### COMMAND (change, `fpq-net-n8` = ws/net-n8)

    flock /tmp/fpq-bench.lock -c 'docker run --rm --shm-size=3g \
      -e FASTPOSTGRES_TRANSPORT=eventfd -e BENCH_GIT_REV=post \
      -v $PWD/bench/internals/threads/ring_scaling.py:/tmp/ring_scaling.py:ro \
      fpq-net-n8 python3 /tmp/ring_scaling.py --rows 100000 --reads 3 --reps 3'

The four controls use the same command and image with one extra `-e`:
`fpq-transport` + eventfd (pre, the same tree before this branch), no
`FASTPOSTGRES_TRANSPORT` (default shm), `FASTPOSTGRES_RINGS_PER_WORKER=1`, and
`PG_OPTS='-c max_worker_processes=16'`.

